Package: sphinx
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Sentinel Safeguard LLC <Sentinelsafeguard@outlook.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), systemd
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/TheRealJesusTheHacker/Sphinx
Description: Sphinx — system-wide ad and tracker blocker (Debian edition, Phase 1)
 Every request gets questioned. Sphinx filters the DNS lookups this
 machine makes: names on its blocklist are answered locally with a
 sinkhole (0.0.0.0), and everything else is forwarded to the upstream
 resolver unchanged. It sees names only — it never inspects, decrypts,
 or modifies the contents of any connection.
 .
 Phase 1 is the working core: the filter daemon (a systemd service),
 the bundled blocklist, and the engage/restore commands that point
 this machine's DNS at the filter and put it back exactly.
 Installing this package never changes your DNS by itself: the
 service is not started or enabled by the install, and turning
 Sphinx on is a separate, explicit step (sudo sphinx engage).
 There is no graphical interface yet, and profiles and list updates
 are later phases. Ads served from the same domain as the content
 itself (YouTube, for example) cannot be blocked by any DNS filter;
 Sphinx does not claim otherwise.
